Hello Durai,

beside the various development systems most (or all ??) serial Bluetooth
Dongles out there are intended for cable replacement and include an upper
layer stack and SPP profile. However, most of them (I think) can be
flashed with a HCI only firmware. But normaly only by the manufacturer.

I don't want to post any advertising here, but may be we can help you.
Please contact me directly if needed.

Best regards,

Peter

On Wed, 1 Jun 2005, Durai wrote:

> Hi,
> I am looking for an UART based bluetooth dongle for my project. From the
> bluez features document,
> I found  this, http://www.digi.com/products/wireless/wavespeeds.jsp .
> But this looks like a UART replacement dongle.
> What I am looking is for is a bluetooth device which can support GAP,
> Serial port,LAN, PAN profiles with bluez support, with
> UART interface. Please help me to find one,
> regards
> durai
